module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_roster_sweep_counts_a_bound_or_label_spelling_as_an_unbound_call

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data a_roster_sweep_counts_a_bound_or_label_spelling_as_an_unbound_call: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_roster_sweep_counts_a_bound_or_label_spelling_as_an_unbound_call" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep emits an import for a row's home in a module where the row's spelling occurs only as a LEXICALLY BOUND reference (a fn parameter) or as an ARGUMENT LABEL, never as a free call to the ambient name. The generated import binds a name the module does not use and sits beside a same-spelled parameter, a shadowing a later resolve may refuse or, worse, silently prefer.",
    "SPECIMEN (NAMESPACE-XL wave 1, PR #14317, 2026-10-18): the home-restricted apply (roster_import_sweep_apply_home_exit home=std.host_text) wrote `import std.host_text { chars }` into test.claim.site_gunb_ai_layout_witness and test.claim.site_gunb_ai_tokens_witness. In both, `chars` is the parameter of `fn var_name_at(s: String, at: Int, limit: Int, chars: List<String>)`, read as `join(chars, \"\")`, and the argument label of the call `var_name_at(s: s, at: at + 6, limit: limit, chars: [])`. No free `chars` call exists in either file. The two edits were reverted by hand in #14317, and this row is the record of why; the defect itself is not repaired there.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: roster_needed_rows counts sites through roster_sites_count, which takes every ScopedReferenceSite whose head classification is HeadLexicallyUnbound and whose spelling is the row's call. The specimen shows that classification reports at least one of the two positions above as lexically unbound -- an argument label is not a reference at all, and a parameter reference is bound by its fn. Which of the two produced the count is NOT established here: the run reported only the resulting EDIT row, not the site that justified it.",
    "SECOND SPECIMEN, A MIS-EDIT (probe on #14338, 2026-10-18): `fn u(chars: fn(String) -> Int, x: String) -> Int { chars(s: x) }` -- a parameter named chars that is itself CALLED -- received both `import std.host_text { chars }` and the relabel `chars(s: x)` -> `chars(text: x)`. The collector reported the parameter's call head as HeadLexicallyUnbound, so the import count and the label plan both took it for the free name; the rename rewrote a call to the parameter, not to the home. The defect is therefore not confined to an unused import.",
    "INTERIM GUARD (tidy-ant-251's ruling C): v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep roster_name_locally_bound refuses home-name-locally-bound for any module that binds a row's call spelling (parameter, let, match binder, lambda parameter), read from the binders themselves; both specimens are enrolled controls that must refuse. The guard only refuses. Its dissolution trigger is this row's trigger. The front-end defect itself is dispatched separately as a chain re-derivation in v2.compiler.lexical_scope / reference_site_collector.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- the generator's own output was inspected and the two edits reverted before commit; nothing mechanical exposed it. HARM if missed: an unused import shadowing a parameter in every module where an ambient name doubles as a local name, generated at sweep scale.",
        "REPAIRED AT THE CLASSIFIER (v2.compiler.reference_site_collector, PR #14435, 2026-10-19): the collector now carries a POSITION fact per site and reads it where a head is classified, so a head sitting at a type annotation, a binder type, a field/argument label or a pattern tag answers HeadNotAValuePosition instead of HeadLexicallyUnbound -- one rule for every non-value position, no shape test per shape. Measured on the SECOND SPECIMEN's fixture through the sweep's own front-end path, every site with its recorded position path: the CALL head `chars` at [u/AB/] reads FRAME both before and after (so the reported symptom did not reproduce -- the value frame was never the broken link), while the site that read UNBOUND was the declaration's OWN BINDER SPELLING in the signature, [u/OS/] `chars` and [u/OS/] `x`, plus the parameter types at [u/a:x/BT/]; those now read NOTVALUE. Controls pinning both readings live in v2.test.claim.lexical_scope (the_called_parameter_head_at_the_call_is_bound_in_the_frame pins sig=notvalue,call=frame; a_parameter_is_not_bound_in_a_sibling_parameter_type and a_type_annotation_sees_no_value_binder were themselves asserting the defect and now assert notvalue). The revert arm is behavioural: with the classifier's consultation of the position authority reverted those three go red and every positive stays green, 25/28 against 28/28, while namespace_xl0.reference_conservation stays 26/26 with byte-identical eval_steps on both sides.",
    "STILL OPEN AFTER THAT REPAIR, so this row does not close: the INTERIM GUARD above is now a second path beside the modeled one and retires in its own PR -- delete v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep roster_name_locally_bound's two call sites (roster_rows_label_plan:816's locally-bound label refusal and roster_sweep_rows:964's RefusalHomeNameLocallyBound import-row refusal), proved by that fn's own three-shape controls plus this row's specimen controls coming back Clean and correctly relabelled with it removed. Two neighbouring defects are named follow-ups, not repaired here: signature mentions that never reach a value frame (a function's own return-type head at [u/] and a free call head at [u/AB/] read UNBOUND whether or not a parameter of that declaration is in scope -- frame threading, not position), and the sweep's import authority: site_head_is_undecided reads scope.imported, so the head answer depends on a CALLER-supplied list -- measured on one fixture, an imported head reads UNBOUND when the caller passes no rows and UNDECIDED when it passes them. All three production call sites do pass rows (v2.compiler.module_acquisition acquisition_identity_checked, v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep roster_label_plan and roster_needed_rows); the no-row readings are the two deliberate no-import fixtures in v2.test.claim.lexical_scope. So the classifier reads imports from a parameter rather than from the tree it is handed, and a caller that forgets the list silently gets free names for imported heads.",
"CEILING: structurally guaranteed. The sweep should count a site only where resolve itself would look the spelling up as a free name: a call-head (or pipe-target) reference that no lexical binder, module declaration or existing import answers, never a label. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: the sweep's needed-row decision reads the same free-name classification resolve uses for the occurrence (v2.compiler.reference_site_collector's head binding, with labels excluded and binders honoured), proved by a roster control whose fixture is the specimen's shape -- a parameter and an argument label spelled like a row's call -- and which must come back Clean. Until then a sweep PR lists every module the generator touched where the spelling has no free call, and reverts it with a citation to this row."
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.reference_site_collector", decl_name: "site_head_binding", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.occurrence_role", decl_name: "reference_position_of", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.occurrence_identity", decl_name: "ReferencePosition", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep", decl_name: "roster_head_is_free", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.module_acquisition", decl_name: "acquisition_head_is_candidate_module", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.lexical_scope", decl_name: "the_called_parameter_head_at_the_call_is_bound_in_the_frame", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.lexical_scope", decl_name: "a_parameter_is_not_bound_in_a_sibling_parameter_type", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.lexical_scope", decl_name: "a_type_annotation_sees_no_value_binder", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
